<misterromdescription>
    <!--
      Sega Model 2 core for MiSTer FPGA - Copyright (C) 2026 alphanu1
      SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

      Super GT 24h (Model 2B-CRX). Derived from MAME 0.289 model2.cpp
      ROM_START(sgt24h), the parent set. For the Model 2B build
      (branch model2b, Model2.sv M2_2B: the ADSP-21062 SHARC as the
      coprocessor); the 2A and 2C cores cannot run it. Study R1024
      (this set's census), R1031.

      MAME 0.289: MACHINE_NOT_WORKING, but R1024's census raced it: a
      4,096-word SHARC program, 165 DM words, nothing past the first
      cut's list; 28 writes to the texture windows' upper MB (mirrored
      on 2B). MAME's init_sgt24h has its two patches commented out:
      none here. The comms program (MAME's cpu4) is not loaded. No
      protection.

      THE 2A LAYOUT (VF2's MRA; no 128 MB module needed), each slot
      zero-padded to its size:
        0x0000000  i960 program 0-512 KB (MAME maincpu 0x000000)
        0x0080000  main_data, 16 MB
        0x1080000  textures, 8 MB (MAME's 0-4 MB and 8-12 MB; 4 MB loaded)
        0x1880000  polygons, 12 MB (8 MB loaded). The 2B core keeps the
                   SHARC's DM page at SDRAM byte 0x2080000, this slot's 8 MB
                   mark, so a 2B set in this layout can have at most 8 MB
        0x2480000  256 KB of zeros (the 2A TGP's tables; 2B has none)
        0x24C0000  68000 sound program, 512 KB
        0x2540000  SCSP samples, 8 MB          -> SDRAM byte 0x3400000
        0x2D40000  i960 program 512 KB-2 MB    -> SDRAM byte 0x2600000
                   (the rest 0 as MAME's region)
      Image: 0x2EC0000 bytes.

      Index 4, the game ID: 0x1C, BORROWED from Over Rev (R928): the
      normal layout and Over Rev's profile, which is MAME's sgt24h
      ports exactly (indy500's with both pedals PORT_REVERSE; IN1 bit
      0 View 1, bit 1 unused here), from the same developer (Jaleco).
      What it implies: Over Rev's comm-board answer at 0x01a04000
      (R928), which this game may or may not poll the same way (not
      measured), and Over Rev's luma table (R932), not one measured on
      this game, so the shading of textured polygons may be off. Bit 7
      is SET in this MRA (0x9C): the 15 kHz CRT flag (R795), which
      starts the core in 15 kHz interlaced whatever the OSD says
      (R908).
    -->
    <name>Super GT 24h [15kHz CRT]</name>
    <setname>sgt24h</setname>
    <rbf>Model2B</rbf>
    <!-- R945: the NVRAM file is the backup RAM (16 KB), "M2EEPROM" and the
         93C46 EEPROM (128 bytes): the game's settings. -->
    <nvram index="2" size="16520"/>
    <rom index="4" md5="none">
        <part>9C 00</part>
    </rom>
    <mameversion>0289</mameversion>
    <year>1996</year>
    <manufacturer>Jaleco</manufacturer>
    <category>Driving</category>

    <rom index="0" zip="sgt24h.zip" md5="none">

        <!-- 0x0000000  i960 program 0-512 KB -->
        <interleave output="32">
            <part name="epr-19155.15" crc="593952fd" map="0021" offset="0x000000" length="0x040000"/>
            <part name="epr-19156.16" crc="a91fc4ee" map="2100" offset="0x000000" length="0x040000"/>
        </interleave>

        <!-- 0x0080000  i960 data, 16 MB -->
        <interleave output="32">
            <part name="mpr-19146.11" crc="d66b5b0f" map="0021"/>
            <part name="mpr-19147.12" crc="d5558f48" map="2100"/>
        </interleave>
        <interleave output="32">
            <part name="mpr-19148.9" crc="a14c86db" map="0021"/>
            <part name="mpr-19149.10" crc="94ef5849" map="2100"/>
        </interleave>

        <!-- 0x1080000  textures, 8 MB (MAME's 0-4 MB, then its 8-12 MB) -->
        <interleave output="32">
            <part name="mpr-19153.27" crc="136adfd0" map="0021"/>
            <part name="mpr-19152.25" crc="363769a2" map="2100"/>
        </interleave>
        <part repeat="4194304">00</part>

        <!-- 0x1880000  polygons, 12 MB (8 MB loaded; the SHARC's DM page is at
                     SDRAM byte 0x2080000, the slot's 8 MB mark) -->
        <interleave output="32">
            <part name="mpr-19150.17" crc="e0ad870e" map="0021"/>
            <part name="mpr-19151.21" crc="e2a1b125" map="2100"/>
        </interleave>
        <part repeat="4194304">00</part>

        <!-- 0x2480000  TGP math tables, 256 KB: none on 2B (no TGP) -->
        <part repeat="262144">00</part>

        <!-- 0x24C0000  68000 sound program, 512 KB (16-bit, byte-swapped) -->
        <interleave output="16">
            <part name="epr-19157.31" crc="8ffea0cf" map="12"/>
        </interleave>

        <!-- 0x2540000  SCSP samples, 8 MB (16-bit, byte-swapped); moved by the
                     loader to SDRAM byte 0x3400000 -->
        <interleave output="16">
            <part name="mpr-19154.32" crc="7cd9e679" map="12"/>
        </interleave>
        <part repeat="4194304">00</part>

        <!-- 0x2D40000  i960 program 512 KB-2 MB (R862) -->
        <interleave output="32">
            <part name="epr-19155.15" crc="593952fd" map="0021" offset="0x040000" length="0x040000"/>
            <part name="epr-19156.16" crc="a91fc4ee" map="2100" offset="0x040000" length="0x040000"/>
        </interleave>
        <part repeat="1048576">00</part>

    </rom>

    <!-- BORROWED ID: Over Rev (Model 2C)'s profile (R928): steering on either
         stick, pedals on the right stick's Y or Accel / Brake (reversed, as
         MAME's sgt24h ports), Shift Up / Down, View 1. -->
    <buttons names="Coin,Start,Test,Service,View 1,-,Accel,Brake,Shift Up,Shift Down"/>
</misterromdescription>
